title: CausticAreaLIDAR
tags:
---
<<playerCantMove Player>> <<setLIDAR RadarTriangle false>>
Bubby: Oh look, we've run into an area of murky water! We can swim through it, but when sediment on the seafloor gets disturbed like this it messes with our LIDAR sensor.[pause=8000 /]
Bubby: Do you know why the LIDAR sensor won't work in murky water?
-> No, do you have any idea why?
    Bubby: Hmm, I think it's because the sediment in the water messes with the LIDAR ray![pause=5000 /]
    Bubby: The light can't pierce the murky water, so it can't tell us about any potential obstacles in the area.[pause=5000 /]
-> Yes I do!
    Bubby: Really? Awesome! Why can't we use LIDAR here?
    -> The sediment blocks with the LIDAR's light ray!
        Bubby: Yeah you're right! Good thinking!
    -> The water is moving too fast for LIDAR to get through!
        Bubby: Good guess, but the water movement won't affect the light ray. The light can't pass through dirt well though, which is why we can't use LIDAR![pause=8000 /]
    -> It takes more energy to use LIDAR with all the dirt around.
        Bubby: Good guess, but the amount of energy needed to make the light ray doesn't change. The light can't pass through all that dirt moving around, which is why we can't use LIDAR![pause=8000 /]
    -> Actually, I don't know. Do you know?
        Bubby: Hmm, I think it's because the sediment in the water messes with the LIDAR ray![pause=5000 /]
        Bubby: The light can't pierce the murky water well, so it can't tell us about potential obstacles within the murky water.[pause=5000 /]
Bubby: I'll start preparing my SONAR sensor - it should be ready once we reach the next area. SONAR can help us navigate big areas of murky water![pause=8000 /]
<<playerCanMove Player>>
===

title: CausticAreaSONAR
tags:
---
<<playerCantMove Player>> <<setLIDAR RadarTriangle false>> <<setSonar SonarPulse false>>
Bubby: Here's another area of murky water! Our LIDAR sensor won't work here - do you remember why?
-> No, can you remind me?
    Bubby: LIDAR won't work because the sediment in the water disturbs with the LIDAR ray! The light can't get through the dirt.[pause=5000 /]
    Bubby: We can use SONAR instead - SONAR can pierce through murky water just fine since it uses sound instead of light! It'll show us if there's anything hiding in here.[pause=8000 /]
-> Yes I do!
    Bubby: Awesome! Why can't we use LIDAR here?
    -> The sediment messes with the LIDAR's light ray!
        Bubby: Yeah you're right! Good thinking! Instead, we can use SONAR to find out if there are things hiding in this area. SONAR can pierce through murky water just fine since it uses sound instead of light![pause=8000 /]
    -> The water is moving too fast for LIDAR to get through!
        Bubby: Good guess, but the speed of the water won't matter to LIDAR since it uses light! LIDAR won't work here because the sediment blocks the light ray before it can show us obstacles.[pause=8000 /]
        Bubby: We can use SONAR instead - SONAR can pierce through murky water just fine since it uses sound instead of light! It'll show us if there's anything hiding in here.[pause=8000 /]
    -> It takes more energy to use LIDAR with all the dirt around.
        Bubby: Good guess, but all this sediment means the light ray can't get through to see if there are obstacles in our way![pause=5000 /]
    -> Actually, I don't know. Can you remind me?
        Bubby: LIDAR won't work because the sediment in the water disturbs with the LIDAR ray! The light can't get through the dirt.[pause=5000 /]
        Bubby: We can use SONAR instead - SONAR can pierce through murky water just fine since it uses sound instead of light! It'll show us if there's anything hiding in here.[pause=8000 /]
<<playerCanMove Player>>
===

title: BubbleVent
tags:
---
<<playerCantMove Player>> <<setLIDAR RadarTriangle false>> <<setSonar SonarPulse false>>
Bubby: Oh look, a bubble vent! We'll have to be careful, bubbles can cause problems with our SONAR sensor.[pause=5000 /]
Bubby: Do you know why bubbles could cause problems for SONAR?
-> No, why might bubbles cause a problem?
    Bubby: SONAR won't work around bubbles because when the sound hits them, it has to move between air and water, which changes the speed it moves at and messes with our ability to measure how fast it comes back to us![pause=8000 /]
    Bubby: We'll need to use LIDAR here instead- bubbles can't block light after all!
-> Yes I do!
    Bubby: Awesome! Why can't we use SONAR when bubbles are around??[pause=5000 /]
    -> The bubbles burst when hit with sound!
        Bubby: Almost but not quite! When sound hits a bubble, it has to move between air and water, which changes the speed it moves at and messes with our ability to measure how fast it comes back to us![pause=8000 /]
        Bubby: We'll need to use LIDAR here instead- bubbles can't block light after all![pause=5000 /]
    -> The bubbles block the sound!
        Bubby: Almost but not quite! When sound hits a bubble, it has to move between air and water, which changes the speed it moves at and messes with our ability to measure how fast it comes back to us![pause=8000 /]
        Bubby: We'll need to use LIDAR here instead- bubbles can't block light after all![pause=5000 /]
    -> The bubbles change the speed of the sound!
        Bubby: That's right! When sound hits a bubble, it has to move between air and water, which changes the speed it moves at and messes with our ability to measure how fast it comes back to us![pause=8000 /]
        Bubby: We'll need to use LIDAR here instead- bubbles can't block light after all![pause=5000 /]
    -> Actually, I don't know. Can you tell me?
        Bubby: SONAR won't work around bubbles because when the sound hits them, it has to move between air and water, which changes the speed it moves at and messes with our ability to measure how fast it comes back to us![pause=8000 /]
        Bubby: We'll need to use LIDAR here instead- bubbles can't block light after all![pause=5000 /]
<<playerCanMove Player>>
===

title: Fish
tags:
